---
alwaysApply: true
---
Never run `eas build`, `eas submit`, `eas update`, `npx expo publish`, `expo export`, or any command that creates a build, submits to a store, or publishes an OTA update on your own initiative, no matter how large the edit. Run them only when the user explicitly asks in the current message. When a change needs a new build and the user has not asked, say so in one sentence and stop. When asked, use `EAS_BUILD_NO_EXPO_GO_WARNING=true npx eas build --platform ios --profile production --auto-submit --non-interactive` (there is no EAS Update channel configured, so JS changes also ship via a build).
